 R←Test_Misc_004(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;c;m;g;parms;filename;report;json;raw;note;CR;LF
⍝ Exercise `SaveCrashRequest` for a message whose header has not been parsed yet.
⍝ That is what a crash inside the server's own parsing of a request leaves behind, and
⍝ `Test_Server_120` cannot reach it: there the request is complete, so `Headers` is
⍝ available and the raw header is not reported.
⍝ Needs neither a server nor a crash: a stand-in with one connection is all it looks at.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 (CR LF)←⎕UCS 13 10
 raw←'GET /%C0 HTTP/1.1',CR,LF,'Host: localhost',CR,LF
 raw,←'Authorization: Bearer Test_Misc_004-secret',CR,LF

 ##.Plodder.⎕SHADOW'G'                              ⍝ Both are locals of `Run` in a running server,
 ##.Plodder.⎕SHADOW'R'                              ⍝ so they must be established here
 ##.Plodder.R←Rumba
 ##.Plodder.G←⎕NS''
 g←##.Plodder.G
 g.Server←⎕NS''
 g.Server.Connections←⎕NS''
 g.Server.Connections.C1←⎕NS''
 c←g.Server.Connections.C1
 c.Tid←⎕TID                                         ⍝ `GetConnectionOfThread` matches on this
 c.PeerAddress←'127.0.0.1'
 c.LastBlock←raw
 m←⎕NS''
 m.Header←raw                                       ⍝ No `Headers`: parsing did not get that far
 m.Method←'GET'
 m.RequestTarget←'/%C0'
 c.Messages←,m

 filename←∆GetTestFolder,'/Test_Misc_004'
 'CREATE!'##.FilesAndDirs.CheckPath ∆GetTestFolder
 parms←⎕NS''
 parms.crashFilename←filename
 parms.addToMsg←''                                 ⍝ That is what `CreateParms` establishes
 ##.Plodder.SaveCrashRequest parms

 →T.PassesIf ⎕NEXISTS filename,'.request.json'
 json←⊃⎕NGET filename,'.request.json'
 ⎕NDELETE filename,'.request.json'
 report←⎕JSON json

 →T.PassesIf'127.0.0.1'≡report.PeerAddress
 →T.PassesIf report.Thread=⎕TID
 →T.PassesIf report.LastBlockLength=≢raw
 →T.PassesIf 1=≢report.Messages
 →T.PassesIf 0=(⊃report.Messages).⎕NC⊂'Headers'      ⍝ The raw header, not name/value pairs
 →T.PassesIf∨/'Authorization: ***'⍷(⊃report.Messages).Header
 →T.PassesIf∨/'Authorization: ***'⍷report.LastBlock
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'Test_Misc_004-secret'⍷json

 note←parms.addToMsg                               ⍝ What the HTML report will show
 →T.PassesIf 2=≢note
 →T.PassesIf∨/'GET /%C0'⍷⊃note
 →T.PassesIf∨/'127.0.0.1'⍷⊃note
 →T.PassesIf∨/(filename,'.request.json')⍷⊃¯1↑note
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'Test_Misc_004-secret'⍷⊃,/note

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
